  "summary": "Open the MySQL database of a running Local WordPress site in TablePro.",
  "description": "A Local add-on that adds a button to the Database tab of a running site. It reads the site's database name, user and password from Local, forwards a port on 127.0.0.1 to the site's MySQL socket, and opens a mysql:// URL for that port in TablePro.\n\nInstall the .tgz from the latest release in Local under Add-ons, Installed, Install from Disk. Needs Local 10 or later.",
